 "script": "SpaceX caught Starship after fourteen laps around Earth. It spent about twenty-two hours in orbit, the Associated Press reported. Then the tower's arms grabbed it in South Texas. It's a first for a ship back from orbit. But the Super Heavy booster missed its catch and exploded. Here's why it matters. SpaceX says Starship can be fully reused. NASA picked it to land astronauts on the Moon. Moon or Mars first? Tell us below.",
